# Build/install into local vault

When you finish implementing or fixing a plugin in this repo, always end by installing into the local Obsidian vault so the user can reload and test.

For Fulcrum:

```bash
npm run build:install -w obsidian-plugin-fulcrum
```

For another plugin package, use that workspace’s `build:install` (same `tooling/install-to-vault.mjs` copy into `.obsidian/plugins/<id>`).

Do this after the change is complete — not instead of tests. Skip only if the session was planning/Q&A with no code changes, or if the user said not to install.
